{title: Savior, Like a Shepherd Lead Us}
{artist: attr. Dorothy A. Thrupp, Hymns for the Young}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune BRADBURY - William B. Bradbury (1859)}
{meta: public_domain Text 1836, tune 1859: both published before 1931 (US public domain); all authors, translators and composers died over 70 years ago. Chords and section layout: original simple arrangement by Tabernacle Tools. Original verses only, no modern additions.}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Savior, like a [G]shepherd [D]lead us, much we need Thy [A]tender [D]care;
In Thy pleasant [G]pastures [D]feed us, for our use Thy [A]folds pre[D]pare.
[A]Blessed Jesus, [D]blessed Jesus! [A]Thou hast bought us, [D]Thine we are;
[D]Blessed Jesus, [G]blessed [D]Jesus! Thou hast bought us, [A]Thine we [D]are.
{end_of_verse}
{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]We are Thine, Thou [G]dost be[D]friend us, be the guardian [A]of our [D]way;
Keep Thy flock, from [G]sin de[D]fend us, seek us when we [A]go a[D]stray.
[A]Blessed Jesus, [D]blessed Jesus! [A]Hear, O hear us [D]when we pray;
[D]Blessed Jesus, [G]blessed [D]Jesus! Hear, O hear us [A]when we [D]pray.
{end_of_verse}
